WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.110
- You go to Rome to have best Italian food

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:06.660
or you go to Japan to get
the best Japanese food.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.720
You would come to Dubai,
you get best of Italy,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.170
you get best of Japan,
you can get best of India.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.540
I would say Dubai is
the most exciting city

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.283
you would find across all the cuisines.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.080
- [Ching] Wherever I am in the world,

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.080
food is the focal point
of everything I do.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.490
My name is Ching, and I'm
a chef and food writer.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.220
My taste journeys have
taken me all over the world

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.280
in search of great
flavors and new recipes.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.590
Finally, it has brought me to Dubai

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.800
and I can't wait to explore
it's rich and varied food scene,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.003
one bite at a time.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.850
Growing up in a Taiwanese household

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.590
meant I ate a lot of spice,

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.690
so I'm excited to discover
what spice combinations

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.640
Dubai's street stalls have to offer

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.930
with another fellow spice
enthusiast, Himanshu.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.440
- [Himanshu] Hi, my name is Himanshu Saini

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.963
and I am a chef from the last ten years.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.570
Currently, I am working
for two restaurants,

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.240
Trèsind and Carnival by Trèsind.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.440
They're both in Dubai.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:07.990
And the third one is in Kuwait

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.290
and the fourth one is
about to open in Mumbai.

00:01:14.141 --> 00:01:15.694
- Hi! Chef?
- Hello, are you Ching?

00:01:15.694 --> 00:01:16.527
How are you?

00:01:16.527 --> 00:01:17.840
Welcome to Dubai.
- Good, how are you?

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.980
- [Himanshu] India also there
is a food truck culture,

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.030
but here it is more elaborate.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.500
There's a place called Last
Exit and they have 10, 15 trucks

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.550
from waffles to hot dogs to burgers.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.340
Street food is one of the
key philosophies at Trèsind.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.800
The experiences that you
get at the street counter,

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.980
this is something which we
want to give to our diners

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.230
in a fine-dine set up.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.020
My first initial memory of food,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.040
my mother along with her six sisters,

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.270
who used to cook together
in a very big house

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.180
feeding almost 50 people a night

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.833
and that is how I got the
first impression about food

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:51.540
because that gives everybody a great joy.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.010
My parents are very proud
of what I have done so far,

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.980
and I feel very proud.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.010
The true meaning of chaat is to lick.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.450
The chaat is so spicy
and tangy that people

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.250
usually they lick their fingers off.

00:02:03.447 --> 00:02:06.330
So this one is the modern
version of the chaat,

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:09.890
so they've added corn, so
they've added potato, tomatoes.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.400
The corn really makes it interesting.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.030
- [Ching] Yeah, it's got
so much texture as well.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.200
- Yes, I think we should
round off this meal

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.160
with a cup of tea?

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.550
- [Ching] Perfect, let's do it.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.520
There's a heart to the
cuisine here in Dubai.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.460
I didn't realize that you could have

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.213
such a vast array of choice.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.340
So this is Project Chaiwala

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.470
and they've got a secret
cinema art house experience

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.490
here in Dubai.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.920
- It's very interesting
that they brought in

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.240
professionals from India.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.880
They've been making teas for years.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:39.980
Chai is such a basic thing,

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:43.450
but nobody has given such
emphasis which these guys have.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.970
It's really great to
see a product from India

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.303
being made in a city like Dubai.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.470
- [Ching] But Dubai's street food scene

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.560
is vast and very tasty,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.570
and naturally it's time to get to see

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.630
Himanchu's take on street food.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.830
- You've seen the traditional
version of the chaat

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:07.200
at the chaat counter, but we
do a very modern version of it.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.283
We're going to paint this canvas
with the chaat ingredients.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:12.833
Just splash the chutneys.

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:14.340
- [Ching] OK.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.173
- Brilliant.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.400
And then we have these spinach
fritters, some crackers,

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.124
and now we're going to top-

00:03:24.124 --> 00:03:24.957
- [Ching] That looks beautiful!

00:03:24.957 --> 00:03:27.450
- [Himanchu] -top it again
with some more chutneys.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.620
And now we're going to freeze
this in liquid nitrogen.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.150
Once we freeze it, it
becomes very brittle,

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.820
and then we crush it on our chaat.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:37.313
We mix it gently and then
we supposed to have it.

00:03:39.278 --> 00:03:40.111
- That is beautiful!

00:03:40.111 --> 00:03:43.030
- [Himanchu] And then we can
get the texture of the papri,

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:46.656
the palak patta, the masala,
there's so much going on here.

00:03:46.656 --> 00:03:47.784
- Thank you so much, chef, you're amazing.

00:03:47.784 --> 00:03:49.540
- Thank you so much, thank you.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.950
Food is one common
language across the world,

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:55.000
it's how it travels from
one country to another.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.933
I think my heart is in India,
but I feel home here in Dubai.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:01.210
- [Ching] I've come to
Dubai because I want

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:04.120
to really experience Dubai culture

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.630
and for me the best way
to explore any culture

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.970
is 100% through food.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:13.380
So there is so much to experience here.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.733
Dubai really is a place for food.

